################################################################################
 THREAT: Route / signal hijacking (DNS hijacking)
################################################################################
 Description   : An attacker changes name resolution so clients connect to a host they control instead of the real service.
 Why relevant  : Sensors and operators reach the services by name (*.ssle.local). A hijacked ingestion name sends every sensor reading to the attacker (data theft/poisoning) and silently stops the real pipeline.
 Exploitation  : Write access to the DNS server's zone file (compromised admin account, bad automation, malicious insider) and a dnsmasq restart; all clients follow immediately.
 Monitoring    : Wazuh syscheck (FIM, realtime) on /etc/dnsmasq-zones: rule 550 'checksum changed' -> rule 100230 (level 12). dnsmasq query log shows who received the bad answer.
 Action-resp.  : restore-dns.sh active response on the DNS agent: copies the golden zone (/etc/dnsmasq.hosts.clean) back and restarts dnsmasq (no timeout, the fix is permanent).
################################################################################

